phi-adapter-thinq (0.1.6-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Broker ACL: appliance topics are matched by client id (%c), not by
    user name. On the certificate listener the user name is the
    certificate's CN, which LG's modules all request as `*.clip.com`;
    the client id is the appliance's uuid.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:02:24 +0000

phi-adapter-thinq (0.1.5-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * D0211: the door is flag bit 0x08, seen opening and closing; 0x02 and
    0x10 are set throughout and unnamed; the salt bit moves out of the
    way to 0x20 until seen.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:58:12 +0000

phi-adapter-thinq (0.1.4-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Dishwasher status as the D0211 really sends it: each block is
    [flag][len] + len bytes (len 0x18), a change record carries the
    previous block first and the current one last. The §5.3 offsets then
    hold: state, process, course 05 = Eco, times as hour and minute.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:03:38 +0000

phi-adapter-thinq (0.1.3-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Acknowledge the appliance's frames the way the cloud does (`ack`
    command, F0 00 <type> 04, plus the sequence for envelopes); answer
    req_timesync with the seven UTC bytes; send a dishwasher the start
    packet after provisioning; note an undeploy. Without the acks a freshly
    enrolled D0211 repeated its identification record and undeployed after
    a few minutes, its Wi-Fi LED dark.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:52:32 +0000

phi-adapter-thinq (0.1.2-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * phi-thinq-routed no longer mints a CA of its own: it signs with the box
    CA phi-mosquitto keeps under /var/lib/phi/tls (--ca-dir, PHI_TLS_DIR)
    and re-issues its own leaf when that CA or the host name changes. The
    8883 listener lives in phi-mosquitto's drop-in now; the example drop-in
    is gone, and the package recommends phi-mosquitto rather than mosquitto.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:20:00 +0200

